{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579909-bad-player-gm-tropes","id":579909,"title":"Bad player/gm tropes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-05T10:24:09-07:00","id":579909,"title":"Bad player/gm tropes","content":"Share your bad experiencia<br /> <br /> I will NEVER dm to otakus...i swear to Cthulhu. I had so many stories of VtM players calling their chars Alucard or modeling their chars after him<br /> <br /> Also from VTM, i had so many bullshit players claiming their chars are Generation 1 .... Just..urghhh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T11:36:18-07:00","id":579999,"title":"","content":"I haven't read Twilight yet, because I'm afraid that there will be some line in it that just jumps out at me as something from an online chat game from the 5 years before it was published. (Though, the online versions tended to be somewhat more gender fluid.)<br /> <br /> There have already been several times when I've wondered how many times Laurel Hamilton has swung through those games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T11:46:40-07:00","id":580021,"title":"","content":"At a gen con larp there was a guy who made a mage called &quot;The Doctor&quot; his foci was a pair of sonic screw drivers, saddest etherite ever","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T13:41:09-07:00","id":580151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579909-bad-player-gm-tropes#post579909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Share your bad experiencia<br /> <br /> I will NEVER dm to otakus...i swear to Cthulhu. I had so many stories of VtM players calling their chars Alucard or modeling their chars after him<br /> <br /> Also from VTM, i had so many bullshit players claiming their chars are Generation 1 .... Just..urghhh</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As an otaku, I'm of the opposite view. I will never DM to Goths or Punks. I like VTM without over-the-top moping, angsting, constant Humanity checks over the slightest of things, and Sisters of Mercy quotes. <br /> <br /> On a more serious note, I hate metaplot purists and anyone who insists the metaplot is mandatory, especially now in the day of the metaplot-neutral V20, is clearly someone I do not wish to play or GM with. Personally, I think the metaplot was a poorly-written and railroady mess (especially in Revised) and I always make it clear that the metaplot does not exist in my games. Gangrel are still in the Camarilla (complete with a Justicar), the Week of Nightmares never happened and the Ravnos are still a full clan, and there was no Red Star, Avatar Storm, or any of those Revised Edition apocalyptic shenanigans, and the Stargazers are still in the Garou Nation. Also, Demon: The Fallen does not exist in my games. <br /> <br /> If V20 is metaplot-agnostic, then my games are metaplot-free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:45:44-07:00","id":580471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579909-bad-player-gm-tropes?p=580151#post580151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As an otaku, I'm of the opposite view. I will never DM to Goths or Punks. I like VTM without over-the-top moping, angsting, constant Humanity checks over the slightest of things, and Sisters of Mercy quotes.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, I hate metaplot purists and anyone who insists the metaplot is mandatory, especially now in the day of the metaplot-neutral V20, is clearly someone I do not wish to play or GM with. Personally, I think the metaplot was a poorly-written and railroady mess (especially in Revised) and I always make it clear that the metaplot does not exist in my games. Gangrel are still in the Camarilla (complete with a Justicar), the Week of Nightmares never happened and the Ravnos are still a full clan, and there was no Red Star, Avatar Storm, or any of those Revised Edition apocalyptic shenanigans, and the Stargazers are still in the Garou Nation. Also, Demon: The Fallen does not exist in my games.<br /> <br /> If V20 is metaplot-agnostic, then my games are metaplot-free.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember the game I was in when Revised started, Vampire and Mage were very developer driven, to the point where at times it came off as 'play our way, or you suck' seemed like a prevalent attitude (especially with the Avatar Storm), and players being on the receiving end of things they couldn't really effect. Werewolf, at least, seemed more player driven and providing plot hooks for players to use. Heck, I think the entire Revised WtA line was spawned from fan feedback. The Stargazers 'leaving' was even presented as 'the NPCs almost nobody ever uses start going to different meetings' with limited impact on characters already in play, and the forming of the Ahadi based on a player driven event (killing Black Tooth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T03:59:40-07:00","id":580735,"title":"","content":"Oh God. Usenet used to be horrible with that. I kinda prefer the devs these days. I think only Malcolm Sheppard sat well with me back then, because even when I didn't agree with him, I felt he'd make a well reasoned point. Oh and back then Stephenls was only a poster, not an author.<br /> <br /> To stay on topic... my pet peeve are people who seem to think that mechanics are a statment about the setting, and that just because something is mechanically valid and advantageous it's a staple of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:00:40-07:00","id":580990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579909-bad-player-gm-tropes?p=580735#post580735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To stay on topic... my pet peeve are people who seem to think that mechanics are a statment about the setting, and that just because something is mechanically valid and advantageous it's a staple of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lupus Stargazer Ahroun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T20:50:09-07:00","id":583138,"title":"","content":"Malkavians, Daughter of Cacophony, Ragabashes and their kind can be game-breakers if you think insanity or &quot;ecsentrism&quot; is an excuse to be silly. A friend of a friend convinced the ST to let him play a DoC and he took the silly, spoiled sugarbaby route that I had to lie to him why everyone else didn't want him to come back.<br /> <br /> Also people who use the game as a way to brag about their OCs, making them the stars while the players are their barely useful sidekicks. (That happened in a d20 game I was in.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T21:07:03-07:00","id":583157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579909-bad-player-gm-tropes?p=580990#post580990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lupus Stargazer Ahroun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh this old splat combo ain't what it used to be, ain't what it used to be, ain't what it used to be...<br /> <br /> (One could also argue about whether or not high Rage is a straightforward mechanical advantage, given its great potential for backfire when at least 63% of all the people you meet that aren't monsters are freaked out by your very presence.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T00:26:10-07:00","id":583249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579909-bad-player-gm-tropes?p=580990#post580990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lupus Stargazer Ahroun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda. That one is mechanically superior, because it's worth a shitload more XP then a Bone Gnawer Homid Ragabash, and is a egregious example, but usually people in Werewolf don't all play Lupus Stargazers (Ahroun or otherwise).<br /> <br /> It's more like the folks who assume that each and every vampire is constantly (ab)using disciplines at each other, and that killing or avoiding them is the only rational response. It's like the folks who play Mage and then seem to live in this bubble where their character have 4-8 hours every day for casting rituals and hanging a gazillion effects on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:57:22-07:00","id":583781,"title":"","content":"Good ol' &quot;I have played this game for 20 years and things ALWAYS have been like this&quot; person. When that obscure LARP thing or a tabletop houserule aren't present in another person's game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:46:35-07:00","id":583939,"title":"","content":"Werecoyotes named Nigel. (It's a long story but... Just no.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T21:00:57-07:00","id":584150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/579909-bad-player-gm-tropes?p=583249#post583249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda. That one is mechanically superior, because it's worth a shitload more XP then a Bone Gnawer Homid Ragabash, and is a egregious example, but usually people in Werewolf don't all play Lupus Stargazers (Ahroun or otherwise).<br /> <br /> It's more like the folks who assume that each and every vampire is constantly (ab)using disciplines at each other, and that killing or avoiding them is the only rational response. It's like the folks who play Mage and then seem to live in this bubble where their character have 4-8 hours every day for casting rituals and hanging a gazillion effects on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The weird thing is, as few Lupus Stargazer Ahrouns I've seen... one could have easily been confused for a Bone Gnawer Ragabash.<br /> <br /> And for the others, some of that can come in easily if someone had the misfortune to start in an offline setting, where there were sites that prided themselves on the body count and Mages were allowed to list some random spheres and do whatever they wanted.<br /> <br /> I actually got kicked out of one game because I said 'woah, I really don't think that's the way Mage works...'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}